    "interpretation": "NOT evidence that the candidate list matches the library. Labels are generated by BioCLIP from this list, so both 'every tag is on the list' and 'every candidate got used' are expected by construction \u2014 the second especially, since argmax over 360 classes across 51766 tags will touch every class even when guessing. Read normalised_entropy instead: near 1.0 means the mass is spread almost uniformly across the list (consistent with guessing), well below 1.0 means it concentrates on particular species (consistent with real signal). Correctness still requires the human label set or an expert check."
